/* Three authored electrical foundations and their explicit, idealized circuit models. */
const FOUNDATION_LESSON_IDS9=['divider-foundation','capacitor-foundation','inductor-foundation'];
const FOUNDATION_DATA9=[
 {id:'divider-foundation',kind:'divider',title:['分压从零开始：阻值、节点与负载','Voltage dividers: resistance, nodes and loads'],pre:['kirchhoff','components'],week:31,
 goal:['从接地端数清下方电阻，计算任意节点电压，并解释为什么接上负载后读数会变。','Count resistance from ground to calculate a node voltage and explain how a connected load changes it.'],
 sections:[
 ['先认清“阻值”，再讨论分压','Start with resistance, not physical size','电阻的阻值用Ω表示，1 kΩ = 1000 Ω。两个电阻“同阻值”指测得或标称的电阻值相同，不是外观、尺寸或材料组织相同。标称1 kΩ还可能有公差；本台先用精确理想阻值。电压必须在两个点之间定义，标成GND的节点被选为0 V参考，不代表任何一个电阻天然拥有某个电压。','Resistance is measured in ohms: 1 kΩ = 1000 Ω. Equal resistance means equal nominal or measured resistance, not equal size, appearance or material structure. Real nominal values have tolerance; this bench starts with exact ideal values. Voltage is a difference between two points. GND is the chosen 0 V reference, not an intrinsic voltage belonging to a resistor.'],
 ['没有分支，串联电流才相同','An unbranched series path has one current','电源正端经过R1、R2回到负端，且中点没有取走电流时，流过两只电阻的电流相同。总阻值为R1+R2，I = Vs/(R1+R2)，各电阻的压降为I乘它自己的阻值。压降相加等于电源电压。先画闭合路径再算，不要把电阻想成按个数平均分配电压的容器。','With a source, R1 and R2 in a single closed path and no current drawn at their junction, both resistors carry the same current. Total resistance is R1+R2, I = Vs/(R1+R2), and each drop is I times that resistor. The drops add to the supply voltage. Draw the closed path first; resistors do not divide voltage by component count unless their resistances match.'],
 ['两只同阻值：中点为什么是一半','Two equal resistors give a midpoint at one half','把两只1 kΩ电阻接在6 V和GND之间。总阻值2 kΩ，电流6/2000 = 0.003 A = 3 mA；每只压降3 V。中点相对GND的电压是下方电阻的压降，因此为3 V，也就是Vs/2。若把两只一起换成10 kΩ，中点仍为3 V，但电流降至0.3 mA；比例相同不等于所有电气行为相同。','Place two 1 kΩ resistors between 6 V and GND. The 2 kΩ total gives 6/2000 = 0.003 A = 3 mA, so each drops 3 V. The midpoint voltage relative to ground is the drop across the lower resistor: 3 V, or Vs/2. Replacing both with 10 kΩ preserves 3 V but reduces current to 0.3 mA. Equal ratios do not imply identical loading or power behavior.'],
 ['三只同阻值：两个节点分别是多少','Three equal resistors create two different nodes','三只1 kΩ串在9 V和GND之间，电流3 mA，每只压降3 V。从上往下，电源节点9 V，R1后节点A是6 V，R2后节点B是3 V，末端GND是0 V。因此A为Vs的2/3，B为1/3。不能说“三只电阻，中间都等于1/3”：1/3是每只电阻的压降比例，节点电压还取决于它距离参考地之间有几只电阻。','Three 1 kΩ resistors between 9 V and GND carry 3 mA and each drops 3 V. From top to bottom the nodes are 9 V, A at 6 V after R1, B at 3 V after R2, then 0 V. A is 2Vs/3 and B is Vs/3. One third describes each individual drop; a node voltage depends on the entire resistance between that node and the ground reference.'],
 ['不同阻值：从GND向上分组','Unequal values: group from ground upward','选一个测点，把电源到测点的电阻合为Rup，把测点到GND的电阻合为Rdown。未接负载时Vnode = Vs × Rdown/(Rup+Rdown)。例如12 V、由上到下1 kΩ、2 kΩ、3 kΩ，节点A下方是2+3 = 5 kΩ，故A = 12×5/6 = 10 V；节点B下方只有3 kΩ，故B = 6 V。分子用下方总阻值，不是随手选一只电阻。','Choose a tap. Combine the resistance from the source to the tap as Rup and from the tap to GND as Rdown. With no load, Vnode = Vs × Rdown/(Rup+Rdown). For 12 V and 1 kΩ, 2 kΩ, 3 kΩ from top to bottom, A has 5 kΩ below it and is 12×5/6 = 10 V. B has 3 kΩ below it and is 6 V. The numerator is the entire groundward resistance.'],
 ['接入负载后，下面变成并联','A load creates a parallel lower branch','把Rload从选中节点接到GND，它与整段Rdown并联。先求Req = Rdown×Rload/(Rdown+Rload)，再求Vnode = Vs×Req/(Rup+Req)。此时上方电流分成下方电阻电流与负载电流，Iup = Idown+Iload，不能再假定每只串列电阻电流都相同。两只1 kΩ跨10 V，中点再接1 kΩ到GND：Req=500 Ω，中点从5 V降到约3.333 V。','Connect Rload from the chosen tap to GND. It parallels the entire Rdown segment. First Req = Rdown×Rload/(Rdown+Rload), then Vnode = Vs×Req/(Rup+Req). Upper current splits: Iup = Idown+Iload. Current through every resistor in the original chain is no longer identical. Two 1 kΩ resistors across 10 V with another 1 kΩ from the midpoint to GND give Req = 500 Ω and about 3.333 V instead of 5 V.'],
 ['分压器可以测信号，不是万能供电器','A divider is not a general power supply','万用表、ADC或后级电路都不是绝对不取电流。输入阻抗很高时，负载影响可能较小；输入电阻接近Rdown时，误差明显。实际ADC还有采样电容和建立时间，不能只看一个直流电阻。分压器适合受控负载下的信号比例，不应直接当作给电机、单片机或变化负载供电的稳压器。','Meters, ADCs and later circuit stages may draw current. A very high input resistance can make loading small; resistance comparable to Rdown makes it significant. Real ADCs also have sampling capacitance and settling requirements, beyond a static resistor model. A divider scales a signal under known loading; it is not a regulator for a motor, microcontroller or changing power load.'],
 ['按预测、测点、负载三步复核','Verify prediction, reference and loading','先在纸上写出Vs、各阻值、所选节点与GND；计算无负载结果，再接入负载观察差值。操作台给出每个节点相对同一GND的电压，读数不是每只电阻两端的压降。最后检查节点A电压减节点B电压是否等于两点之间的电阻压降。真实搭建还需要核对电阻功率、公差和仪表输入范围。','Record Vs, each resistance, the tap and GND on paper. Calculate the unloaded voltage, then attach a load and compare. Bench node labels all reference the same GND; they are not the individual resistor drops. Check that A minus B equals the drop between those nodes. Real construction also needs resistor power, tolerance and instrument input-range checks.']
 ],example:['三只电阻由上到下1、2、3 kΩ，Vs=12 V，取节点B。Rup=3 kΩ，Rdown=3 kΩ，无负载B=6 V。再接Rload=3 kΩ：Req=1.5 kΩ，B=12×1.5/4.5=4 V。Iup=12/4.5k=2.667 mA；Idown=4/3k=1.333 mA；Iload=1.333 mA。A=12−2.667 mA×1 kΩ=9.333 V。','For 1, 2, 3 kΩ from top to bottom at 12 V, tap B has Rup=3 kΩ and Rdown=3 kΩ, so unloaded B=6 V. Add Rload=3 kΩ: Req=1.5 kΩ and B=12×1.5/4.5=4 V. Iup=2.667 mA, Idown=1.333 mA and Iload=1.333 mA. A=12−2.667 mA×1 kΩ=9.333 V.'],
 error:['三只同阻值的每只压降为1/3，但两个节点对地分别为2/3和1/3；有负载时要重新计算。','Three equal resistors each drop one third, but their internal nodes are at two thirds and one third of supply. A load changes the calculation.'],
 task:[['为一个高阻输入选择分压测点，随后检查意外负载的影响。','Choose a divider tap for a high-impedance input, then investigate an unexpected load.'],['9 V与三只同阻值的两个节点各是多少？换成1、2、3 kΩ和12 V会怎样？','Where are both nodes with 9 V and three equal resistors? What changes for 12 V and 1, 2, 3 kΩ?'],['依次使用两只同阻、三只同阻、不同阻值和负载预设；每次先写预测，再记录两个节点读数与电流。','Use the equal-two, equal-three, unequal and loaded presets. Predict each case first, then record node voltages and currents.'],['用从GND向上的Rdown解释结果，并核对负载接点的电流守恒。','Explain each result using groundward Rdown and check current conservation at the loaded tap.'],['自己设定一个非整数比例，先算无负载与有负载两种情况，再用台面验证。','Choose a new non-integer ratio; calculate unloaded and loaded cases before testing.'],['保存四组条件、预测、节点读数和一条负载电流等式。','Keep four parameter sets, predictions, node readings and one current-balance equation.'],['能分清节点电压与单只压降；独立计算负载等效阻值，三项电流误差只来自显示舍入。','Distinguish node voltage from resistor drop and independently calculate the parallel load; any current-balance mismatch is only display rounding.']],
 refs:[{title:['Analog Devices：分压器与负载','Analog Devices: voltage dividers and loading'],url:'https://www.analog.com/en/resources/glossary/voltage-divider.html'}]},
 {id:'capacitor-foundation',kind:'capacitor',title:['电容从零开始：储能、初始电压与RC','Capacitors: energy, initial voltage and RC response'],pre:['components','power','divider-foundation'],week:35,
 goal:['解释电容为什么储能、为什么电压不能在有限电流下瞬间跳变，并计算带初始电压的充放电。','Explain capacitor energy and voltage continuity under finite current, then calculate charging and discharging from a nonzero initial voltage.'],
 sections:[
 ['两片导体，中间是绝缘介质','Two conductors separated by a dielectric','理想电容有两个导体与中间的绝缘介质。外部电路把电荷从一侧转移到另一侧，两极板出现等量异号电荷，能量储存在电场中。理想模型没有电子直接穿过绝缘层的导电通路；外部两端仍能在充放电过程中出现电流。示意图的正负符号表示板上净电荷，不是完整的微观粒子模拟。','An ideal capacitor has two conductors separated by an insulating dielectric. The external circuit redistributes charge, leaving equal and opposite net charges on the plates; energy is stored in the electric field. There is no conducting electron path through an ideal dielectric, yet terminal current flows while charge changes. The diagram shows net plate charge, not a microscopic particle simulation.'],
 ['电容量是每伏能分离多少电荷','Capacitance relates separated charge to voltage','Q = C×Vc。C的单位F，Q的单位C（库仑），不要把电容符号C和电荷单位C混为一谈。100 µF = 0.0001 F，在5 V时单块极板电荷量的绝对值为0.0005 C = 500 µC。电容量越大，在同样电压下分离的电荷越多；电容不是“固定装着某个电压”的电池。','Q = C×Vc. Capacitance uses farads (F), while charge uses coulombs (C); the symbol C for capacitance is not the charge unit. A 100 µF capacitor is 0.0001 F. At 5 V, the magnitude of either plate charge is 0.0005 C = 500 µC. Higher capacitance stores more separated charge at the same voltage; a capacitor is not a battery with a fixed voltage.'],
 ['为什么电压要接着上一刻走','Why voltage continues from the previous instant','对恒定电容，电流i = C×dVc/dt。有限电流只能让电压以有限速度变化；把电压瞬间跳到另一个值需要理想的冲激电流。接电源的瞬间，电容电压从原来的V0开始，不能无条件当成0 V。电阻限制起始电流，i(0+) = (Vs−V0)/R；如果V0高于Vs，起始电流方向会反过来。','For constant capacitance, i = C×dVc/dt. Finite current produces a finite rate of voltage change; an instantaneous voltage jump would require an ideal current impulse. On connection, voltage starts from its existing V0, not automatically zero. A resistor limits initial current to (Vs−V0)/R. If V0 exceeds the source voltage, the initial current reverses.'],
 ['RC：快慢由电阻和电容量一起决定','RC sets the speed of approach','简单串联RC的时间常数τ = R×C，必须先把kΩ换成Ω、µF换成F再算秒。10 kΩ与100 µF给出τ=1 s。朝固定目标电压Vtarget变化时，Vc(t)=Vtarget+(V0−Vtarget)e^(−t/τ)。经过1τ，剩余差距约为起始差距的36.8%；5τ仍剩约0.67%，不是数学上恰好完成。','The simple series RC time constant is τ = R×C. Convert kΩ to Ω and µF to F before obtaining seconds. With 10 kΩ and 100 µF, τ=1 s. Toward a fixed target, Vc(t)=Vtarget+(V0−Vtarget)e^(−t/τ). After one time constant, about 36.8% of the initial gap remains; after five, about 0.67% remains rather than exactly zero.'],
 ['充电、放电和断开是三种不同情形','Charging, resistor discharge and isolation differ','充电时目标通常是Vs；本台切到放电时，电源被移出回路，而电阻与电容仍组成闭合放电环路，目标为0 V。切换瞬间电压保持原值，电流可以改变方向。若真的把理想电容两端完全隔离，没有泄漏路径，它会保留电压，不会按本台的RC放电曲线下降。真实电容有泄漏，测量仪表也可能消耗电荷。','Charging targets Vs. In this bench, Discharge removes the source while leaving a closed resistor-capacitor loop targeting 0 V. Voltage is continuous at the switch, while current may reverse. A truly isolated ideal capacitor with no leakage path retains its voltage; it does not follow this resistor-discharge curve. Real capacitors leak, and a connected measuring instrument can also remove charge.'],
 ['储能随电压平方变化','Energy depends on voltage squared','电容能量E = ½CV²。100 µF、5 V对应0.5×0.0001×25 = 0.00125 J = 1.25 mJ。若电容量不变而电压加倍，能量变成四倍。通过电阻放电时，原先储存的能量逐渐变成电阻的热；曲线下的电压面积不是能量，不能把V·s直接当成焦耳。','Capacitor energy is E = ½CV². For 100 µF at 5 V, it is 0.5×0.0001×25 = 0.00125 J = 1.25 mJ. Doubling voltage at fixed capacitance quadruples energy. During resistor discharge, stored energy becomes heat in the resistor. The area under a voltage-time curve is not energy: V·s is not a joule.'],
 ['实际用途：旁路、滤波和时序','Applications: bypassing, filtering and timing','电源附近的旁路电容可以在短暂变化期间提供或吸收电流，使局部电压变化减小；它的作用受容量、布线电感和ESR影响。RC低通把快速变化衰减，但这与“电容永远让电流通过”不是同一句话。直流达到稳态后，理想电容电流为0；启动、纹波和负载变化属于随时间变化的过程。','A bypass capacitor near a supply can source or absorb transient current and reduce local voltage change. Capacitance, wiring inductance and ESR all matter. An RC low-pass attenuates rapid changes, which does not mean a capacitor always conducts. At DC steady state an ideal capacitor has zero current; startup, ripple and load changes are time-dependent processes.'],
 ['从模型走向真实器件','Moving from the model to a real part','实际电容有额定电压、容差、漏电、等效串联电阻与温度范围；部分类型有极性。这里使用理想恒定电容量，不模拟击穿、极性损坏和热。先学会辨认单位与初始电压，再按器件资料选择参数；不要把网页中的随意调参当作真实器件允许承受的条件。','Real capacitors have voltage ratings, tolerance, leakage, equivalent series resistance and temperature limits; some types are polarized. This model uses constant ideal capacitance and omits breakdown, reverse-polarity damage and heat. Learn units and initial state first, then use the part datasheet for selection. A webpage parameter range is not a rating for a physical component.']
 ],example:['R=10 kΩ、C=100 µF、Vs=5 V、V0=2 V，τ=1 s。1 s后Vc=5+(2−5)e⁻¹≈3.896 V，电流约(5−3.896)/10000=0.1104 mA。此时切到放电，起点仍是3.896 V；再过1 s约为1.433 V，不能重新从5 V或0 V开始。','With R=10 kΩ, C=100 µF, Vs=5 V and V0=2 V, τ=1 s. After 1 s, Vc=5+(2−5)e⁻¹≈3.896 V and current is about 0.1104 mA. Switch to resistor discharge at that instant: it starts at 3.896 V. One second later it is about 1.433 V, not a new curve starting at 5 V or zero.'],
 error:['“直流稳态像开路”不是说电容一接电就没有电流；暂停动画也不代表真实电路能暂停时间。','An ideal capacitor is open at DC steady state, not necessarily at startup. Pausing an animation is not a physical ability to pause a circuit.'],
 task:[['观察一个有初始电压的RC电路怎样接近目标，再在途中切换放电。','Observe an RC circuit with an initial voltage and switch it to discharge partway through.'],['初始2 V、目标5 V，经过1τ会到多少伏？切换放电时哪一个量不能跳变？','From 2 V toward 5 V, what is the voltage after one τ? Which quantity remains continuous at discharge switching?'],['设置10 kΩ、100 µF、初始2 V，单步1τ核对结果；开始播放，再切换放电，观察切换前后电压。','Set 10 kΩ, 100 µF and initial 2 V; advance one τ to check the value. Start playback, then switch to discharge and compare voltage before and after.'],['用当前电压作为下一段的初始条件，解释电流符号与电场储能如何变化。','Use the current voltage as the next segment initial state and explain current sign and electric-field energy.'],['把C加倍，从同一初始条件重做，比较1秒后读数和时间常数；区分相同秒数与相同τ。','Double C and repeat from the same initial state. Compare readings after one second and compare time constants; distinguish seconds from multiples of τ.'],['记录参数、初始状态、1τ电压、切换时电压以及两次电流方向。','Record parameters, initial state, voltage after one τ, voltage at switching and both current directions.'],['能从非零V0计算充放电，解释电压连续与电流可跳变，并正确把µF换成F。','Calculate from nonzero V0, explain voltage continuity and possible current jumps, and convert µF to F correctly.']],
 refs:[{title:['OpenStax：RC电路与充放电','OpenStax: RC circuits and charging/discharging'],url:'https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/10-5-rc-circuits'},{title:['OpenStax：电容中的储能','OpenStax: energy stored in a capacitor'],url:'https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/8-3-energy-stored-in-a-capacitor'}]},
 {id:'inductor-foundation',kind:'inductor',title:['电感从零开始：磁场、电流连续与RL','Inductors: magnetic fields, current continuity and RL'],pre:['components','kirchhoff','power','capacitor-foundation'],week:37,
 goal:['认识线圈的电感、磁场储能与绕组电阻，计算RL电流，并解释关断时为什么需要续流路径。','Recognize inductance, magnetic energy and winding resistance, calculate RL current and explain the need for a current-decay path.'],
 sections:[
 ['电感是什么，为什么常做成线圈','What inductance means and why coils are useful','导线中有电流就会产生磁场。把导线绕成线圈并选择磁芯，可以让磁通与电流的联系更强。电感L描述磁链随电流的关系，单位H（亨利），1 mH = 0.001 H。简单线性模型中L固定；真实磁芯可能饱和，L还可能随电流与频率变化，不能只凭线圈外观猜数值。','Current in a conductor creates a magnetic field. Winding a coil and selecting a core can strengthen the link between current and magnetic flux. Inductance L relates flux linkage to current and is measured in henries: 1 mH = 0.001 H. A linear model uses constant L; real cores can saturate and inductance may vary with current and frequency. Appearance alone does not determine its value.'],
 ['电感两端电压取决于电流变化','Inductor voltage depends on changing current','采用电流从标“+”端流入的被动符号约定，理想电感vL = L×di/dt。若1 H电感电流每秒增加2 A，vL=2 V；若以同样速度减少，vL=−2 V。负号说明电压极性相对于标记翻转，并不是电流必须立即反向。电感反抗的是电流变化，不是把所有电流都挡住。','With current entering the terminal marked positive, an ideal inductor obeys vL = L×di/dt. A 1 H inductor increasing at 2 A/s has 2 V across it; decreasing at the same rate gives −2 V. The negative sign reverses the marked voltage polarity, not necessarily the current direction. Inductance opposes changes in current rather than blocking all current.'],
 ['有限电压下，电流不能突然跳变','Finite voltage implies continuous current','对恒定L，瞬间改变电流需要理想冲激电压。因此接电源前若i=0，刚接上时仍从0 A起步；若之前已有电流，也必须从那个值继续。电感电流是状态，不能像一个随手开关的动画参数。相对地，电感两端电压可以在切换时跳变；这与电容电压连续、电流可跳变形成一组对应。','For constant L, an instantaneous current change requires an ideal voltage impulse. If current is initially zero, it starts at zero when the source is connected. Existing current must continue from its previous value. Inductor current is a state, not an arbitrary on/off animation setting. Voltage can jump at switching, complementary to capacitor voltage continuity and possible current jumps.'],
 ['RL时间常数与最终电流','RL time constant and final current','串联电源、电阻和理想电感，令Rtotal为回路全部串联电阻，τ = L/Rtotal，最终电流I∞ = Vs/Rtotal。一般式i(t)=I∞+(I0−I∞)e^(−t/τ)。例如L=1 H、Rtotal=10 Ω、Vs=5 V，τ=0.1 s，I∞=0.5 A，从0开始经过1τ约为0.3161 A。R变大使最终电流变小，也使该RL时间常数变小。','For a source, resistor and ideal inductor in series, Rtotal is all series resistance, τ = L/Rtotal and final current I∞ = Vs/Rtotal. Generally i(t)=I∞+(I0−I∞)e^(−t/τ). With 1 H, 10 Ω and 5 V, τ=0.1 s and I∞=0.5 A; starting at zero, current after one τ is about 0.3161 A. Increasing R lowers both final current and this RL time constant.'],
 ['直流稳态：理想短路不等于真实零电阻','DC steady state: ideal short, real winding resistance','直流稳态时di/dt=0，因此理想电感部分vL=0，可在该稳态电路里当作短路。但真实线圈的铜线有绕组电阻Rw，会产生iRw压降和i²Rw损耗。外接10 Ω、绕组2 Ω、5 V时最终i=5/12≈0.4167 A，理想电感压降0 V，整个线圈端电压约0.8333 V。还没到稳态时，不能提前把电感短接。','At DC steady state di/dt=0, so the ideal inductive part has vL=0 and behaves as a short in that steady-state circuit. Real copper windings have resistance Rw, giving an iRw drop and i²Rw loss. With an external 10 Ω, winding 2 Ω and 5 V, final current is 5/12≈0.4167 A. The ideal inductive drop is zero, but the complete coil terminal voltage is about 0.8333 V. This short-circuit approximation does not describe startup.'],
 ['关断后，电流从哪里走','Where current goes after source removal','本台切到衰减回路时移除电源，却保留电阻、绕组与电感的闭合路径。已有电流最初仍沿原方向流，i=I0e^(−t/τ)，理想电感电压变成−iRtotal来维持逐渐减小的电流。如果直接断开一个没有合适续流或钳位路径的真实线圈，可能产生很高的电压；本台不会把这种复杂开断过程伪装成电流瞬间归零。','The decay setting removes the source but preserves a closed path through the resistor, winding and inductor. Existing current initially keeps its direction and decays as I0e^(−t/τ). Ideal inductor voltage becomes −iRtotal. Opening a real energized coil without an appropriate freewheel or clamp path can generate high voltage. This bench does not disguise that more complex interruption as an instantaneous current reset.'],
 ['能量在磁场里，大小与电流平方有关','Magnetic energy is proportional to current squared','在线性理想模型中，E = ½Li²。0.1 H里有2 A时能量为0.5×0.1×4=0.2 J，电流加倍能量变为四倍。续流衰减时电感释放磁场能量，在本台中变成串联电阻与绕组的热。图里的磁力线仅表示场强趋势，不给出真实空间磁场分布，也不能据此计算磁芯温升。','For an ideal linear inductor E = ½Li². At 2 A in 0.1 H, energy is 0.5×0.1×4=0.2 J. Doubling current quadruples energy. During closed-loop decay, stored magnetic energy is released into the series and winding resistances. The field drawing shows a trend, not a spatial field solution or a calculation of core temperature.'],
 ['把RC和RL放在一起比较','Compare RC and RL without mixing their states','电阻把电能转成热，不独立储存理想电路状态；电容储电场能，记住电压，τ=RC；电感储磁场能，记住电流，τ=L/R。选择滤波、继电器驱动和电机续流元件时，要知道哪个状态不能突然改变。真实设计还要核对额定电流、饱和电流、绕组温升和开关钳位，不能只看一个H数值。','A resistor dissipates electrical energy rather than storing an independent ideal circuit state. A capacitor stores electric-field energy and remembers voltage, with τ=RC. An inductor stores magnetic energy and remembers current, with τ=L/R. Filters, relay drivers and motor freewheeling require knowing which state cannot jump. Real selection also checks current ratings, saturation, winding temperature and switching clamps, not just inductance.']
 ],example:['L=1 H、R=10 Ω、Rw=2 Ω、Vs=5 V，从0 A开始：τ=1/12≈0.08333 s，I∞=5/12≈0.41667 A。1τ后i≈0.26338 A，vL=5−12i≈1.83940 V，线圈端电压vcoil=vL+2i≈2.36616 V。此时切到衰减回路，电流仍为0.26338 A，而vL立刻变为−12i≈−3.16060 V，随后逐渐趋于0。','With L=1 H, R=10 Ω, Rw=2 Ω and Vs=5 V from zero: τ=1/12≈0.08333 s and I∞=5/12≈0.41667 A. After one τ, i≈0.26338 A, vL=5−12i≈1.83940 V and coil-terminal voltage vcoil=vL+2i≈2.36616 V. Switching to the decay loop preserves 0.26338 A, while vL immediately becomes −12i≈−3.16060 V and then tends toward zero.'],
 error:['电感反抗电流的变化；理想直流稳态压降为0不等于真实线圈没有电阻。停止并复位是重新设定实验初态，不是开断线圈的物理过程。','An inductor opposes current change. Zero ideal steady-state voltage does not mean a real coil has no resistance. Stop and reset reinitializes the experiment; it does not model physically opening an energized coil.'],
 task:[['研究一只带绕组电阻的线圈，比较接通与闭环衰减。','Study a coil with winding resistance during source connection and closed-loop decay.'],['1 H、外接10 Ω、绕组2 Ω、5 V时，τ与最终电流是多少？切到衰减哪一个量保持连续？','For 1 H, external 10 Ω, winding 2 Ω and 5 V, what are τ and final current? What stays continuous when switching to decay?'],['先设Rw=0求1τ电流，再设Rw=2 Ω重启实验；单步1τ后切换衰减，记录电流和理想电感电压。','Start with Rw=0 and find current after one τ. Restart with Rw=2 Ω; step one τ, switch to decay and record current and ideal inductor voltage.'],['分别解释理想电感压降与整个线圈端电压，说明负vL为何不要求电流立即反向。','Explain ideal inductive voltage versus complete coil voltage and why negative vL does not require immediate current reversal.'],['设定一个非零初始电流，预测其是上升还是下降；改变外接电阻后重新实验验证τ。','Set a nonzero initial current and predict whether it rises or falls. Change external resistance in a new experiment and verify τ.'],['提交两组Rtotal、τ、I∞与1τ读数，以及切换前后电流/电压对比。','Keep two sets of Rtotal, τ, I∞ and one-τ readings plus current/voltage immediately before and after switching.'],['会计算总电阻，能解释电流连续、理想vL和线圈端电压，并识别闭环衰减与直接开断的差别。','Calculate total resistance and explain current continuity, ideal vL, coil voltage and the difference between a closed decay path and direct interruption.']],
 refs:[{title:['OpenStax：RL电路与续流衰减','OpenStax: RL circuits and current decay'],url:'https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/14-4-rl-circuits'},{title:['OpenStax：磁场中的储能','OpenStax: energy in a magnetic field'],url:'https://openstax.org/books/university-physics-volume-2/pages/14-3-energy-in-a-magnetic-field'},{title:['Coilcraft：电感选型、绕组电阻与饱和','Coilcraft: inductance, winding resistance and saturation'],url:'https://www.coilcraft.com/getmedia/d4009ece-69be-49a6-9185-9cbacb65e3aa/doc469_selecting_inductors.pdf'}]}
];
